														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1362068">
									

<blockquote>
<p>I totally don't buy that they managed to translate it from such a miniscule corpus.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Concur. Linguistically speaking, you need a <strong><em>massive</em></strong> amount of text side-by-side with the same message in a known language in order to get a valid translation. (There's a reason the message I wrote in <a href="/scp-1050">SCP-1050</a> is so long!) The Rosetta Stone is quite long (the English translation is ~470 words, depending on the version of the translation), and up until it was discovered, nobody could read Egyptian hieroglyphs, despite the fact that they adorned countless monuments and artifacts throughout Egypt. It took having the same text side-by-side with Demotic (which had been translated) and lowest Ancient Greek (also translated). The reason it was significant historically is that the text in the other two languages was identified as being the same, which allowed Jean-François Champollion to deduce that the hieroglyphs were saying the same thing.</p>
<p>There are plenty of languages out there which have not yet been deciphered and translated, since no common reference has been discovered. Even if you go with the fact that this is supposed to be some binary or mathematically based language, you'd be presented the same problem. Example:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>9999991837&#160;2978049951&#160;0597317328&#160;1609631859&#160;5024459455<br />
3469083026&#160;4252230825&#160;3344685035&#160;2619311881&#160;7101000313<br />
7838752886&#160;5875332083&#160;8142061717&#160;7669147303&#160;5982534904<br />
2875546873&#160;1159562863&#160;8823537875&#160;9375195778&#160;1857780532<br />
1712268066&#160;1300192787&#160;6611195909&#160;2164201989&#160;3809525720</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Simply presented with this, it would be difficult to know what exactly is meant, unless you had some frame of reference. I've picked a set of numbers that <em>has</em> a pattern known to humans but with a single error to make it not Google-able. I admit I'm not a PhD in mathematics, but I've more than a little practice with cryptography, and I'd have trouble with this one. (Answer beneath the collapsible.)</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>It's digits 762-1101 digits of pi, starting at the Feynman point. The error is the digit &quot;1&quot; after the first six &quot;9&quot;s.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

